WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.840
The Ling ten check samples access to speech sounds across low, middle, and high frequencies.

00:00:06.415 --> 00:00:10.415
It is a brief monitoring tool, not a complete diagnostic assessment.

00:00:11.295 --> 00:00:14.495
First make sure the child understands the response task.

00:00:15.055 --> 00:00:19.855
Then present sounds without visual speech cues, using a normal speaking voice.

00:00:20.535 --> 00:00:23.815
Detection asks whether the child heard something.

00:00:24.275 --> 00:00:26.995
Identification asks which sound was heard.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:32.620
Record those separately, along with the ear or device condition and distance.

00:00:33.465 --> 00:00:38.185
Begin close and in quiet, then increase distance when the task is reliable.

00:00:38.695 --> 00:00:44.215
If a child who previously responded to all the sounds begins missing some, investigate the change.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:51.110
Device trouble, a hearing change, or a middle-ear problem are possibilities, not conclusions from this check alone.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:57.880
Document the pattern and involve the audiologist when the difficulty persists.

